The finding includes site actions for the maintainer: a sentence on the a₀ card giving the chance-match rate, and a "no fixed relation; the redshift slope is the test" sentence.

**So what?** This closes the last place "one equation" could have hidden a cross-sector prediction, and gives the reason. The two sectors share x/(x+2) and nothing else. The one bet a shared knee would make is already losing, conditional on one systematic. The lesson that carries over: a numerical match at one moment is cheap, and the redshift slope it implies is what can actually be tested.

